From a4e15caa2951097ee82dcb762b7f35fe656729f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gao <gao@local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:03:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat: lock cedarx/codec2/mediaplayerservice/widevine
 stack to 32-bit

Allwinner ships these libraries only as 32-bit Android (bionic)
prebuilts. The aarch64 blobs under library/toolchain-sunxi-* link
against glibc/musl for Tina Linux, not Android, so they cannot be
used here. Pin the whole media stack 32-bit; their 64-bit framework
consumers reach them over Binder/HIDL.

- libcedarc/library: 27 prebuilt blobs (libVE, libvideoengine,
  libvdecoder, libvencoder, libcdc_base, libOmxVdec, libOmxVenc,
  libscaledown, libvenc_*, libawh264/265, libawvp9, ...) collapsed
  to a single androideabi_32 src and compile_multilib:32. The
  bogus 'arm64: srcs: androideabi_64/X.so' blocks that pointed
  arm64 at the (nonexistent) 64-bit directory are removed.
- libcedarc/config: root cc_defaults pinned to compile_multilib:32;
  the inherited libcdc_config_defaults covers the source-tree
  modules (base, memory, ve, vdecoder, vencoder, openmax, demo).
- libcedarx/config: same via libcdx_config_defaults; the ~68
  cedarx modules (libcore/*, android_adapter/*, stream/*, parser/*,
  demo/*) all inherit this.
- libcodec2/components: pinned compile_multilib:32 (the -mfpu=neon
  flag in libcodec2_hw-defaults is 32-bit ARM only; the impl
  links libVE/libvideoengine/libcdc_base).
- libmediaplayerservice + its two test modules: MediaPlayerFactory.cpp
  hard-links AwPlayer/AwMetadataRetriever from libcedarx; mediaserver
  is already prefer32 upstream.
- hardware/aw/widevine/Android.mk: dropped the 64-bit blocks that
  referenced lib64/ which does not exist; the 32-bit prebuilts and
  the prebuilt liboemcrypto (level-1 gated, level 3 here) remain.

Three source-level fixes that were caught by -Werror=format once the
64-bit build started type-checking:

- audio_hw.c:2140 - %d -> %zu for size_t bytes argument.
- trans_info.c:181 - %d -> %ld for the pointer difference (size_t
  on the display side).
- rtt.cpp:699 - %lld -> %" PRId64 " with <inttypes.h> for
  wifi_timespan (int64_t).
